# libcuda binaries the sigscan tests and the arm64 survey run on. Read by cmt-sigscan fetch; nothing listed here is
# committed: the files land in tmp/drivers/<arch>/<version>/ (gitignored) and are DATA - never executed, never sourced.
#
# The sole table-membership list: table rows generate C++; survey rows are fetch-only.
# Columns (whitespace separated, one driver per line):
#   arch     x86_64 | aarch64 (the ELF machine, not the Debian name: amd64 = x86_64, arm64/sbsa = aarch64)
#   version  the libcuda version, also the suffix of libcuda.so.<version>
#   url      the package to download: an apt .deb, or NVIDIA's .run installer (download.nvidia.com/XFree86) for a
#            version that is in no apt repository. A .run is never executed: drivers.rs reads its makeself
#            header as text and cuts the compressed tar out of it (see run_payload there).
#   sha256   of the downloaded file. For apt packages it is the SHA256 field of the repository's Packages.gz, whose own
#            hash is in the repository's InRelease, which carries NVIDIA's signature (key 3bf863cc, fingerprint
#            EB69 3B30 35CD 5710 E231  E123 A4B4 6996 3BF8 63CC; checked with gpgv on 2026-11-01 for the three indexes
#            below). For a .run it is the hash in NVIDIA's <url>.sha256sum (fetched 2026-11-01 over HTTPS; not
#            signed, so weaker than the apt chain: TLS to download.nvidia.com is the whole trust). The downloader
#            downloads that .sha256sum again before every .run download and stops if it no longer equals this column.
#   member   path of libcuda inside the package's data.tar.* (.deb) or inside the .run's payload tar
#   libcuda  sha256 of the extracted libcuda.so.<version>: the identity of the binary the offsets belong to. The
#            tables (src/gen/versions_db.inc) are cmt-sigscan's static scan of exactly these files; `cmt-sigscan
#            verify` scans them again and requires the same tables.
#   purpose  table | scanned | survey. `table` rows are in the hook's default tables; `scanned` rows are generated
#            the same way, but the hook uses them only with MEMCPY_HOOK_ALLOW_UNVERIFIED_ROWS=1. `survey` rows are
#            fetched and scanned, never turned into rows. Neither table nor scanned is hardware validation.
#
# x86_64: NVIDIA's CUDA apt repository, ubuntu2404/x86_64 (InRelease signed 2026-10-29). 575.64.05, 595.99.02 and
# 615.78.08 are in none of NVIDIA's apt repositories (ubuntu2004/2204/2404, debian12/13 checked) and come from their
# .run installers.
# Coverage from CUDA 12.8 GA (570.86.10) to the newest release: every x86_64 libcuda release in ubuntu2404/x86_64
# (InRelease signed 2026-11-05; gpgv, same key) and every Linux-x86_64 .run in download.nvidia.com/XFree86 that is in
# no apt repository (2026-11-06). ubuntu2204 and debian12 list no further versions; debian13 is signed by a different
# key (02182E60...) and adds none. 570.181 has no .run on download.nvidia.com (only its .sha256sum); its URL is
# NVIDIA's us.download.nvidia.com mirror, whose .sha256sum is identical. Where one version exists twice, the binaries
# match: 570.148.08 -0ubuntu1/-1ubuntu1, 615.71.09 -1ubuntu1/-2ubuntu1, 580.178.04 apt/.run (sha256, 2026-11-06).
x86_64  570.124.04  https://download.nvidia.com/XFree86/Linux-x86_64/570.124.04/NVIDIA-Linux-x86_64-570.124.04.run  1b786a4b7122d7c4216c58ae4007688a4f778c196c148d919163815ee10d53c4  ./libcuda.so.570.124.04  aa597f392b1f50a30d3fbdf313cabecf0a7b3ca0e969b4a5813b0bdd51e7626d  scanned
